{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/436499-wolf-blooded","id":436499,"title":"Wolf-blooded","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-10T18:28:57-07:00","id":436499,"title":"Wolf-blooded","content":"Hey all<br /> First of al, I love the new 2nd edition. I think my favorite part is the section on wolf blooded. I have all of the WTF 1st Ed books and was wondering if I should have a few players start out as wolf blooded then thru the first few sessions have them turn into werewolves. When they change would they keep any of the merits they had as a wolf blooded <br /> Really toying with adding bale hound or skin changer kin as antagonists as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:33:57-07:00","id":436523,"title":"","content":"I ran a Vampire game that started the players off as ghouls before they became vampires. I know it's not the same thing, but it worked out really well. I was told it helped them appreciate how monstrous a vampire could seem to mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T18:36:21-07:00","id":436528,"title":"","content":"Second Edition's storytelling chapter has some guidelines and ideas for having the players run young Wolf-Blooded who may or may not undergo the First Change at a later point. Check it out!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T02:37:31-07:00","id":436861,"title":"","content":"Hey! Wolf-blooded are great.<br /> <br /> Im already running a WB chronicle that will turn to full-on Werewolf as we go along.<br /> It has been nothing but good fun. Last week we upgraded to 2E, as we had only used what we knew was coming and some house rules from 1E before.<br /> It was quite fun to see that a lot of the Tells we used was almost the same we developed for our game.<br /> I think WB game gears players up to playing Werewolf. But It does not have to be taken in that direction. Wolf-Blooded can become invaluable to a pack in their roles.<br /> Also Some players might like the way a Wolf-Blooded operates in a pack.<br /> <br /> Most of our stories have been more like Sons of Anarchy meets Justified with supernatural horror clawing in here and there.<br /> Seeing IC the WB taking down a Shartha (A Shrizaku) was really cool. No Uratha to help? need to keep the flock from being infected? Send in the Wolfblooded! :-)<br /> <br /> The Storytelling part is quite nice. Also the material related to Wolf-Bloded paint them to have important roles to fill in a pack. Players help enforce this at the start of chargen.<br /> WB are full pack members. they might not do Siskur-Dah but they take care of the flock, they protect Loci, they make sure there is money flowing into their territory and taking care of business in general.<br /> <br /> All I can say is: jump in and get gaming! :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/860-ephraim","name":"Ephraim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar860_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-11T06:04:36-07:00","id":436931,"title":"","content":"Thank you Aiden and Ephraim.<br /> I am loving the new take on WB and am excited to use them in my upcoming stories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer: WtF Night Horrors: Shunned by the Moon<br /> United States Sailor, First Responder,Ally, Bad Speller, Book Hoarder and all around Nerd.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2640-rx781a","name":"rx781a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2640_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}